<description>
Recolor the row-wise passage indicated by wall pixels with the singleton marker color.

Input structure:
- A dominant background contains one singleton marker pixel and one wall color.
- Wall pixels lie on several rows and form left/right limits around the marker column.
- Empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows are open horizontal passages.

Rule:
- On a wall row, paint background pixels between the nearest wall strictly
  left of the marker column and the nearest wall at or right of it; if only
  one side is present, paint from that wall to the opposite grid edge.
- On empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows, paint the whole row.
- On empty rows outside the wall-row band, reuse the nearest end wall-row interval.
- Preserve wall pixels and the original marker pixel.

Key insight:
- The wall color defines scanline limits relative to the marker column; the
  marker color fills those implied horizontal spans rather than flood-filling
  through connected background.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "one singleton marker pixel and rows of wall-color pixels on a dominant background",
  "transform": "recolor background pixels in the scanline passage selected by the marker column: wall rows fill between nearest wall limits, empty interior rows fill full width, and empty exterior rows reuse the nearest end interval"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 11-12 rows x 11-12 cols, single bg color filling most cells
  colors: 3 distinct -- bg (dominant), wall, marker (all different)
  marker:
    count: exactly 1 pixel
    position: inside the wall band, on an empty or wall row; col strictly between wall boundaries on rows that have both sides
  wall:
    pixel_count: 8-14
    rows: 4-6 rows carry wall pixels; they span a contiguous band of 5-7 rows with 1-2 empty interior rows
    per_row: 1-4 wall pixels per wall row; each side (left/right of marker col) forms a contiguous horizontal block of 1-2 pixels
    shape: passage narrows at band endpoints and widens toward the center (lens/funnel); left boundary decreases then increases, right boundary increases then decreases; same-side wall pixels on adjacent wall rows must 8-connect (column step <= 1)
    openings: exactly the intended top/bottom/left/right gaps may separate wall arcs; wall pixels form exactly four 8-connected components and no extra breaks inside adjacent same-side wall rows
    one_sided: some wall rows may have wall only on one side of marker col (passage extends to grid edge) [observed]
    vertical_symmetry: wall pattern is vertically symmetric around band center [observed, not always exact]
  band_padding:
    rows_above_top_wall: 2 [observed]
    rows_below_bot_wall: 3-4
  output_same_size: true
  transform: |
    On each wall row, fill bg pixels between nearest left wall (exclusive) and nearest right wall (exclusive) with marker color; one-sided rows fill to grid edge.
    Empty rows inside band get full-width fill.
    Rows outside band reuse the nearest endpoint wall-row interval.
    Wall pixels and original marker pixel are preserved.

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (constraints are easy to satisfy forward)
  steps:
    - Pick grid size 11-12 x 11-12, choose 3 distinct colors for bg/wall/marker
    - Choose marker column (3-8, leaving room for walls on both sides)
    - Build wall band of 5-7 rows starting 2 rows from top; leave 1-2 empty interior rows near the center
    - For each wall row, place a contiguous block of 1-2 wall pixels on each side of marker col (or one side only rarely); ensure passage widens from endpoints to center while same-side blocks in adjacent wall rows touch 8-neighbor-wise
    - Place marker pixel on any row within the band (empty or wall row) at the marker column
    - Fill remaining cells with bg color
